{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qb2CxxMgiPxV4Z47iLPBGg","type":"tool_result","content":"3:Recording: automatic transcript, excerpt. Speaker detection may be wrong where people talk over each other.\n12:[00:01:24] Ozan Er: Hi. Sorry, my camera is off, the internet here is a bit weak today.\n15:[00:01:33] Burcu Tan: Ours was like that last year, three weeks. Good luck.\n21:[00:02:08] Ozan Er: And the remaining automatic payment, if there is one, before the due date.\n26:[00:02:30] Selin Aydın: Yes. And if the due date is today, it should say today. Not the date.\n27:[00:02:35] Ozan Er: \"Borçlarınız için son ödeme tarihiniz bugündür.\" Okay, we have that.\n29:[00:02:41] Deniz Arı: Second small one from us. After the debt is read, if the customer has more than one card, what comes first, the other-card question or the offer? E-mail and the week change.\n71:[00:07:00] Selin Aydın: Good. So I put the open points in yellow, there are, let me count, eleven? Twelve. We don't have to do all of them today but the edge cases I really want to close because Deniz's team is already building.\n84:[00:08:09] Burcu Tan: I have something but let me check it first, I'm not sure what the IVR does today exactly. I'll look while you continue.\n95:[00:09:11] Kerem Yalçın: And I think it should say why. Not just \"I'm transferring you\". The customer tried three times, they should hear that we can't help right now.\n96:[00:09:18] Deniz Arı: So something like \"Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum\" and then the transfer?\n101:[00:09:38] Kerem Yalçın: No, there nothing went wrong. There it's just the transfer.\n113:[00:10:36] Ozan Er: So it doesn't answer the question, it just transfers. What does it say? Turkish, I assume, since the call is Turkish.\n171:[00:15:17] Burcu Tan: So in the IVR today, after the third no-input, we don't send them to the main menu. We hang up. There's a sentence, then disconnect.\n185:[00:16:31] Deniz Arı: The timing, how many seconds is a silence, that we can leave for another day I think. We have a default.\n206:[00:18:03] Selin Aydın: Okay, statement week. The cut-off date change.\n208:[00:18:09] Selin Aydın: Yes. So in the IVR today... Burcu, you tell.\n209:[00:18:13] Burcu Tan: In the IVR today the customer can change the statement week once a month, and at most three times in a year. Those are the error prompts we have, \"ayda bir\", \"yılda üç\". You have them in my prompt sheet.\n232:[00:20:16] Selin Aydın: Yes. If two cards share one statement, a main card and a linked card, changing the week of one changes the other too. In my document, the assistant says it after the customer confirms. Like, \"okay, changed, and by the way this also affected your other card\".\n252:[00:21:54] Deniz Arı: Yes. And one detail: if there's no registered e-mail at all, we don't offer the e-mail. We only offer the week change, if the customer has the right.\n262:[00:22:40] Deniz Arı: Up to three calming replies. If the customer calms down, we continue the flow. If after three they're still complaining, then \"Sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.\" and transfer.\n265:[00:23:00] Ozan Er: No, never. It doesn't react to the insult. Only calming replies, and if the customer asks for an agent directly, we transfer right away, that's separate.\n285:[00:25:00] Deniz Arı: Statement week: once per calendar year. Not offered if the right is used. Mentioning the limit is optional. Kerem checks the pre-check service with Mert.\n293:[00:25:51] Deniz Arı: I'll send it, maybe not today, tomorrow or Friday.\n297:[00:26:04] Kerem Yalçın: Anything else? The [inaudible] mobile app topic we do next week, not today.\n298:[00:26:09] Selin Aydın: Next week, yes. Ah, and Elçin, mandatory texts, is there anything the assistant must say at the start?\n301:[00:26:24] Deniz Arı: One more for us, sorry, thirty seconds. When the debt service doesn't answer, an error, we go to an agent, not main menu. Still okay?\n313:[00:27:05] Selin Aydın: Is it okay for you if the document only catches up next week? I have the quarterly report this week and honestly...\n314:[00:27:11] Deniz Arı: No problem. We have our notes from today."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abc9990b-2e37-4da6-87b0-3f0fa959dc15","uuid":"aad8aa87-7a40-4e9f-a77f-9fb4f059ce90","timestamp":"2026-10-11T17:55:24.479Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"3:Recording: automatic transcript, excerpt. Speaker detection may be wrong where people talk over each other.\n12:[00:01:24] Ozan Er: Hi. Sorry, my camera is off, the internet here is a bit weak today.\n15:[00:01:33] Burcu Tan: Ours was like that last year, three weeks. Good luck.\n21:[00:02:08] Ozan Er: And the remaining automatic payment, if there is one, before the due date.\n26:[00:02:30] Selin Aydın: Yes. And if the due date is today, it should say today. Not the date.\n27:[00:02:35] Ozan Er: \"Borçlarınız için son ödeme tarihiniz bugündür.\" Okay, we have that.\n29:[00:02:41] Deniz Arı: Second small one from us. After the debt is read, if the customer has more than one card, what comes first, the other-card question or the offer? E-mail and the week change.\n71:[00:07:00] Selin Aydın: Good. So I put the open points in yellow, there are, let me count, eleven? Twelve. We don't have to do all of them today but the edge cases I really want to close because Deniz's team is already building.\n84:[00:08:09] Burcu Tan: I have something but let me check it first, I'm not sure what the IVR does today exactly. I'll look while you continue.\n95:[00:09:11] Kerem Yalçın: And I think it should say why. Not just \"I'm transferring you\". The customer tried three times, they should hear that we can't help right now.\n96:[00:09:18] Deniz Arı: So something like \"Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum\" and then the transfer?\n101:[00:09:38] Kerem Yalçın: No, there nothing went wrong. There it's just the transfer.\n113:[00:10:36] Ozan Er: So it doesn'