{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PoDL772PPEQHRRvoRcqRbJ","type":"tool_result","content":"29\t[00:02:41] Deniz Arı: Second small one from us. After the debt is read, if the customer has more than one card, what comes first, the other-card question or the offer? E-mail and the week change.\n30\t[00:02:51] Selin Aydın: Hm. I'd say other card first. The customer called for the debt. If they have another card, maybe they want that one too.\n31\t[00:02:58] Deniz Arı: So: \"Başka bir kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek ister misiniz?\" and only when the cards are done, or they say no, the offer.\n32\t[00:03:05] Selin Aydın: Yes. Let's confirm with Kerem but I think he'll agree.\n33\t[00:03:09] Burcu Tan: And if they have only one card, you don't ask the other-card question, obviously.\n34\t[00:03:13] Deniz Arı: No, then straight to the offer.\n35\t[00:03:15] Ozan Er: And the offer only has what the customer can actually do. That's why we keep asking about the e-mail and the yearly right, it's connected.\n36\t[00:03:21] Selin Aydın: Yes, we'll get to that, it's in the yellow list.\n37\t[00:03:24] Ozan Er: Okay.\n38\t[00:03:26] Deniz Arı: The amounts, that's clear, I think. Lira and kuruş in full, like \"bin iki yüz lira elli kuruş\", and if kuruş is zero we don't say \"sıfır kuruş\".\n39\t[00:03:35] Selin Aydın: Yes. And the foreign currencies with cents. Sterlin with pence, um, \"peni\".\n40\t[00:03:40] Ozan Er: Yes, we did that already.\n41\t[00:03:42] Burcu Tan: Can I ask something off topic, sorry. Selin, the training on Thursday, is it still on?\n42\t[00:03:47] Selin Aydın: Which one? The onboarding group?\n43\t[00:03:49] Burcu Tan: The onboarding group, yes. I have two people starting.\n44\t[00:03:52] Selin Aydın: I think so. I'll check and write you.\n45\t[00:03:54] Burcu Tan: Thanks.\n46\t[00:03:56] Ozan Er: One more on the card question. The example card names in \"Hangi kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek istersiniz? Örneğin, [kart adı] veya [kart adı] diyebilirsiniz.\" Those are the customer's own cards, max two, right?\n47\t[00:04:07] Selin Aydın: Yes. Never a card the customer doesn't have. It would confuse them.\n48\t[00:04:11] Ozan Er: Okay.\n49\t[00:04:12] Deniz Arı: And after the customer picks the card, we go to the debt. No \"okay, continuing with your Yıldız card\" sentence.\n50\t[00:04:18] Selin Aydın: No, that's not needed. The card name is in the first sentence of the reading anyway.\n51\t[00:04:23] Deniz Arı: Exactly.\n52\t[00:04:24] Selin Aydın: Okay. Let me open the edge cases, so we're ready when Kerem joins. Let me just... the sharing is not... one second.\n53\t[00:04:31] Burcu Tan: We see your mail.\n54\t[00:04:33] Selin Aydın: Oops. Okay. Now?\n55\t[00:04:35] Burcu Tan: Now a white page.\n56\t[00:04:37] Selin Aydın: It's loading. The file is big.\n57\t[00:04:40] Ozan Er: [inaudible] ...every time.\n58\t[00:04:43] Selin Aydın: Sorry?\n59\t[00:04:44] Ozan Er: Nothing, I said the same happens to me every time with that tool.\n60\t[00:04:48] Selin Aydın: [laughs] Okay. I'll stop sharing until Kerem is in.\n61\t\n62\t[...]\n63\t\n64\t[00:06:41] Kerem Yalçın: ...no, it's fine, the other meeting ran late, sorry. Can everyone hear me?\n65\t[00:06:44] Deniz Arı: Yes, loud and clear.\n66\t[00:06:45] Burcu Tan: You're a bit echoey Kerem.\n67\t[00:06:47] Kerem Yalçın: Hm. Better? I switched to the headset.\n68\t[00:06:49] Burcu Tan: Better, yes.\n69\t[00:06:51] Selin Aydın: Okay so, um, I'll share my screen. Can you see the document? The statement debt one, the September analysis.\n70\t[00:06:58] Ozan Er: Yes, we see it.\n71\t[00:07:00] Selin Aydın: Good. So I put the open points in yellow, there are, let me count, eleven? Twelve. We don't have to do all of them today but the edge cases I really want to close because Deniz's team is already building.\n72\t[00:07:13] Deniz Arı: Yes, that would help a lot. Most of our questions are in the edge case part anyway. The happy path is quite clear.\n73\t[00:07:20] Selin Aydın: Okay. Then let's start with, um, silence. Because that one I wrote quickly and I'm not happy with it.\n74\t[00:07:27] Selin Aydın: Right now it says if the customer is silent three times, we go to the main menu.\n75\t[00:07:32] Kerem Yalçın: That's what we agreed in September, no?\n76\t[00:07:34] Selin Aydın: That's what I wrote, yes.\n77\t[00:07:36] Kerem Yalçın: I think it's fine. Main menu, they can choose something else there.\n78\t[00:07:40] Ozan Er: Can I ask one thing about the first two? What does the assistant do on the first silence? Because the document only talks about the third.\n79\t[00:07:47] Selin Aydın: Ah. Good point. It repeats the question, I'd say.\n80\t[00:07:50] Ozan Er: The whole question or a short version?\n81\t[00:07:53] Selin Aydın: Short. Like, it asked which card, the customer says nothing, it asks again shorter. Not the whole sentence with the examples.\n82\t[00:08:00] Ozan Er: Okay, so silence one, short repeat. Silence two, short repeat. Silence three...\n83\t[00:08:05] Kerem Yalçın: Main menu. Let's keep it, we can come back if Burcu has something.\n84\t[00:08:09] Burcu Tan: I have something but let me check it first, I'm not sure what the IVR does today exactly. I'll look while you continue.\n85\t[00:08:15] Kerem Yalçın: Okay.\n86\t[00:08:17] Selin Aydın: Next one. Unclear answer. Or the customer refuses to give the information, like we ask the last four digits and they say \"why do you need it\", that kind of thing.\n87\t[00:08:26] Deniz Arı: For us these are the same branch. The question is asked again and the customer gets three tries. After three, main menu. Is that okay?\n88\t[00:08:33] Selin Aydın: Three tries per question, yes. That matches what we do in the IVR."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abc9990b-2e37-4da6-87b0-3f0fa959dc15","uuid":"72806c27-057e-4b1d-aa7d-9d3aac57b278","timestamp":"2026-10-11T17:55:27.890Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Burak\\